title: Russian troops invade Ukraine!
subtitle: It is war...
new-page: true
on-arrival: ukraine_seen = 1; ukraine_war = 1; foreign_moderation += 0.5; issue_antimilitarism -= 0.4*(dissent); urban_qol -= 3; east_qol -= 4; youth_qol -= 2; rural_qol -= 3; unemployment += 0.1; inflation += 1.5; economic_growth -= 0.5;
view-if: year = 2022 and month >= 2
set-bg: img/ukraine1.jpg
face-image
max-visits: 1
on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/ukrainenyt.webp";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);  
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}
priority: 1

= War in Ukraine

After a failed ultimatum to <span style="color: [+ ukraine_color_1 +];">Ukra</span><span style="color: [+ ukraine_color_2 +];">ine</span>, <span style="color: [+ russia_color_1 +];">Ru</span><span style="color: [+ russia_color_2 +];">ss</span><span style="color: [+ russia_color_3 +];">ian</span> President Vladimir Putin has declared the start of a **special military operation** with the stated goal of protecting the Donbass Republics and ethnic Russians and <span style="color: #753f16;">denazifying</span> the Ukrainian state.  

  
- @cap: It is the nature of capitalism...
- @do_something: We must do something to stop the suffering...

@cap

Perhaps this is simply one of the periodic crises of capitalism. Perhaps this moment will simply pass.

@do_something
on-arrival: crisis_urgency += 1

What can we do to staunch the workers' suffering? It is becoming a hotly debated question.
